MMALProbe - can RISC OS talk to the VideoCore's video decoder?
===============================================================

Step 2 towards hardware H.264 decoding in Reel on every Raspberry Pi
from the Pi 1 to the Pi 4. VCHIQProbe showed how RISC OS's VCHIQ module
is used (BCMSound and BCMVideo use it); this uses it the same way to
reach MMAL, the firmware's media service, and asks about its video
decoder:

  1. opens the "mmal" service;
  2. creates the video decoder ("ril.video_decode");
  3. reads its control, input and output ports: their formats and the
     buffers they want;
  4. asks which encodings its input takes (H.264 is the one we want;
     on a Pi 1, 2 or 3 with the licences, MPEG-2 and VC-1 too);
  5. destroys the decoder and closes the service.

Nothing is decoded and no memory is shared with the VideoCore. If the
firmware doesn't answer, each step gives up after 3 seconds.

Running it:
  Double-click Probe. A window shows the report, which is also saved as
  Result in this directory. Please send Result back; one from an older
  Pi (1, 2, 3 or Zero) too would be very useful.

If the machine locks up (it shouldn't), switch it off and on again.

Needs: RISC OS 5 on a Raspberry Pi, with the VCHIQ module (in the ROM).
